### Coordinator rulings (binding; Book 8 inherits these)
- **Deployment since the Line: TWENTY-SEVEN at book end.** Twenty-three after the Stair; then at the Hall on the 119th the read under water (24), Compression taken standing (25), an Anchor point laid by hand in the breach and held (26); and on the 120th Tide on Oryn, asked and granted, one sitting (27). The Anchor point set as a trial on the 118th is NOT counted ("I'll not call a trial a use"), which agrees with the protected inventory: Anchor used twice this year, once each way (the Stair's unbinding; the Hall's holding). Self-readings are not counted. **Shadow was not used**; it has been used exactly twice in the book and remains sealed; Oryn does not know Seln is its source.
- **The debt is paid.** Three self-readings on three different days (the 102nd; the night of the 119th; before light on the 120th), then all of it told to Oryn at once, and she was read only with her leave. **"The still place"** — Cael's private log label since Books 5–6 — is now a LOCATED finding in him and has been said aloud: to Oryn first, and to the other four on the 121st. Shape and sensation only: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log." No theory, no source, nothing about before.
- **Teague is neither read nor asked** and knows nothing of the mechanism. He forfeited the four-mark weir slip to come (it was never set or paid); the axe-head hold's fence (forty) passes to the five for the cold term ("Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road," / "Ours,"); "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew is unnamed, the older healer of no Path included.
- **The fourth site:** not entered, not named, its effect on a Path UNKNOWN and untested. Lira stopped one pace above the iron; the cordon's bars mark the line; nobody crossed and no sigil was tried. No watch-post; no dating on the cordon; the silhouette is ambiguous. Four stakes have been seen in all, each alone at an edge.
- **The sites and the line:** the Ring (the Fallow), the Stair, the Hall, and the fourth, taken as lying on one line "as near as this skin can show"; no compass bearing is claimed for the whole. Only two maker sentences exist outside protected text: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) and "a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." Karis's hypothesis is still unstated; her window ends on the pencil stopping.
- **Sheets: fifty-two** (eleven Ring, twenty-nine Stair, twelve Hall). The survey kit is on the table at Lowmarch: the case in tarred canvas, a cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke and the bar and a bright turned point, never driven, and a mallet; the dead man's ledger, shut, is Karis's (Seln gave it to her). The case of Seln's is shut and untouched; nothing is decoded.
- **The end, at Lowmarch:** first snow on the 129th; the last ferry on the 130th with two letters west (Hesk; Vell) and Ephram's deferred to the first boat of the thaw; ninety-six in hand; nine lines in Pike's book and no number against the season; eleventh on the cloth; the ferryman's rope still owed. The instruments read true in Cael's hand.
- **Bodies:** Lira's left arm slung and holding nothing, her right ankle never mended; her order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"); Oryn's crossbow is with Lira with ONE bolt left. Brom's shoulder opened, was mended a second time and is BOUND, not mended a third ("It will not hold three times this season"). Cael's three old ribs took Compression again (ten days; quiet on the 129th).
- **Oryn** went north from the fork on her own terms, three weeks late at the oxen ford; an old woman's knee at Thornwater is promised "after the thaw"; her letter is printed once. Her mule and the grey jenny are with the crew.
