editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-56.md:95:"No. I'd none on the ridge, and I've none now."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-56.md:185:"No."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:1:# Chapter 60 — Alignment
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:187:"No. You've said." She set a strip of clean bark down on the scrubbed plank, and a pot of the hold's ink, and a pen cut from a goose quill. "There it is, all the same."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:1:# Chapter 55 — Twice
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:231:"No. You'll be saying *no banks* with a bank under your hand, and *doesn't move* with something that does. A person says a thing truer when the other kind is in front of him." She pushed back her left cuff. "It's my wrist. You know what comes next."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:259:"No. That's outside me. It stops your count at four, and it lets all ten of mine by as if there were no line there. This is inside. It stops nothing, and nothing of mine will cross it."
