     6	- **The sites and the line:** the Ring (the Fallow), the Stair, the Hall, and the fourth, taken as lying on one line "as near as this skin can show"; no compass bearing is claimed for the whole. Only two maker sentences exist outside protected text: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) and "a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." Karis's hypothesis is still unstated; her window ends on the pencil stopping.
     7	- **Sheets: fifty-two** (eleven Ring, twenty-nine Stair, twelve Hall). The survey kit is on the table at Lowmarch: the case in tarred canvas, a cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke and the bar and a bright turned point, never driven, and a mallet; the dead man's ledger, shut, is Karis's (Seln gave it to her). The case of Seln's is shut and untouched; nothing is decoded.
     8	- **The end, at Lowmarch:** first snow on the 129th; the last ferry on the 130th with two letters west (Hesk; Vell) and Ephram's deferred to the first boat of the thaw; ninety-six in hand; nine lines in Pike's book and no number against the season; eleventh on the cloth; the ferryman's rope still owed. The instruments read true in Cael's hand.
     9	- **Bodies:** Lira's left arm slung and holding nothing, her right ankle never mended; her order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"); Oryn's crossbow is with Lira with ONE bolt left. Brom's shoulder opened, was mended a second time and is BOUND, not mended a third ("It will not hold three times this season"). Cael's three old ribs took Compression again (ten days; quiet on the 129th).
    10	- **Oryn** went north from the fork on her own terms, three weeks late at the oxen ford; an old woman's knee at Thornwater is promised "after the thaw"; her letter is printed once. Her mule and the grey jenny are with the crew.
