    86	36. **KEEP — The pass (306th).** Seln's reconnaissance (the shelf, the rig, nine or more, three crossbows). "It's through." The doctrine is told to Teague's four; **the young one's whole-head nod**. **The tall woman's first words to the six in a year.** The wall is set as a lean-to slant. Brom's forearm is bolted before the wall goes up. The pine and stack fall down the plane and close the mouth behind them. The scree is swept clean. Seln climbs. The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge; the young one drags him and is **killed by the sixth volley**, a stride outside the plane. Oryn's hands on him: the first time they come off with nothing done. The name is said once. Seln goes over the lip at the seventh volley. **Cael's first use of Force** on the second stack's brace (stone, along the shelf); the recoil stops in the ribs. Teague takes the stair left-handed. The tall woman reverses her spear. The team breaks east along the ridge, none taken. Vastin goes down; Karis sits with her hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels. "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't." At the far mouth Cael understands the line was not drawn in ink.
    87	37. **KEEP — The plain's edge (306th).** The burial at the east mouth by Teague's crew, with the six carrying at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn on the ribs: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." No term tonight. **Rune turned inward deliberately:** bones; a floor with nothing built on it; an instruction with no language; "the same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." Told to no one. The Arbiter unchanged. The instruments read wronger; the trend is up. The log (§10, "the whole year").
    88	38. **KEEP — The court (307th).** It lies low, and the plain is worn down to it. 1,012 m across (159 cords). The stratum under everything. The first cut ("The others are copies"). The bearing ends, with no sixth. The council. **At the line:** every sigil dark at the same stride; the reactions: Lira's "Right."; Brom pricing the stump; Karis's "It's the first one."; Seln's count; Vastin's line (§10). Oryn steps in one stride: "Nothing. Everything, round it. Same as you." It is unanswered. Teague steps in one stride and steps back: "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough … Field's mine. This isn't field." The turning begins. Lira's fixed exchange. "Wait here."
    89	39. **KEEP — The centre (307th dusk).** 506 strides. Rune turned on the floor at a hundred strides gives the same reading. The eyes are paid. **No edge, no seam.** "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made." He fit. It was not an accident. The third sentence goes unsaid. Oryn reads him at the line ("May I?"): "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He told nobody. The count. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
    90	40. **KEEP — The ledger, the letter, and the dawn (307th night–308th).** Teague goes west carrying the letter; Oryn goes north; "Six. Six and no mule."; Vastin is unadmitted; "West." The closing prose (§10).
