+# VERDICT: CLOSE
+
+Scope: the full current Movement 8 (chapters 53–60) is ready to close with no manuscript line fixes. One sentence in the coordinator's draft `LEDGER-RULINGS.md` and several already-flagged Book 8 entry artifacts need coordinator-side reconciliation; the surviving Book 7 prose is the correct side of each discrepancy.
+
+## (1) Brief items
+
+Baseline used throughout: `state/movement-008/pre-repair-r1/`, not `pre-repair/`. `diff -U0` shows no author change in chapters 53 or 55 and bounded changes in chapters 54 and 56–60.
+
+### A. Lira's left arm at the Hall — RESOLVED
+
+The brace now belongs to the wall, right shoulder and right knee. The left arm stays inert.
+
+- `chapter-54.md:253`, old: "Behind her right shoulder the wall rose a foot higher ... she set her shoulder against that, and laid the stock across her knee."
+- `chapter-54.md:253`, new: "The knee and the coping held the bow between them, and her right hand had only a lever to mind."
+- `chapter-54.md:257`, old: "Her left arm came up, under the wool, to steady the thing."
+- `chapter-54.md:257`, new: "Her left arm lay where a healer had tied it, high against the collar-bone, and did not stir."
+
+Both shots remain, Seln still spans the bow, and the repair does not shorten the action into a summary.
+
+### B. The coda says things once — RESOLVED
+
+The repeated injury, gait, route and still-place explanations have been cut or compressed while all changes of state remain.
+
+- `chapter-59.md:23`, old: "He woke at every turn of the watch with the three old breaks as plain to him as three fingers laid on his side."
+- `chapter-59.md:21`, new: "They were no worse on the road. They only spoke; and he counted a healer's ten days off against them each night, as a man counts off a sentence."
+- `chapter-59.md:47`, old: "A healer had refused that joint once, on arithmetic, and a girl had made up her mind that she would not ask for it a second time ..."
+- `chapter-59.md:45`, new: "They spoke of the foot, and the boot, and the tape; and the name of the joint itself went all the way from a fence of iron to a river without being spoken by anybody."
+- `chapter-60.md:117`, old: "There were ten, and none had a side. And among them was a place where nothing moved, which all of them went round."
+- `chapter-60.md:115`, new: the paragraph stops after "what the same step had found in himself."
+
+The coda still carries Seln's handover of the field ledger (`chapter-59.md:95–117`), Pike's blank season column (`chapter-59.md:177–215`), Oryn's arrival at Thornwater (`chapter-60.md:125–165`) and the six-bowl letter (`chapter-60.md:207–219`).
+
+### C. Around the protected inventory — RESOLVED
+
+The new approach identifies the entry and explains why it is being made tonight; the exit no longer repeats it.
+
+- `chapter-60.md:33`, old: "He ruled a line beneath, and wrote the rest slowly, since it was to stand through a cold term."
+- `chapter-60.md:33`, new: "What came next was the inventory, which he made at the start of anything: every fragment that he carried, in the order of its coming, with the Path that it stood beside and the person who had given it." The paragraph then establishes the first roof he means to return to and the count for the whole season past the Line.
+- `chapter-60.md:43`, old: "He read it through once."
+- `chapter-60.md:43`, new: "He shut the book on it."
+
+The protected inventory at `chapter-60.md:35–41` is unchanged and exact.
+
+### D. Joins after the coordinator's nineteen line fixes — RESOLVED
+
+- The trial Anchor point is expressly uncounted: "Not counted in the number. I'll not call a trial a use" (`chapter-53.md:387`); the next count is twenty-three (`chapter-53.md:389`). Nothing says twenty-eight.
+- The Hall lead-in now names the kerb once as "the hall's outer coping" (`chapter-54.md:315`). Brom asks from three strides out on the grey path, supported under his left arm, with his coat black from shoulder to belt (`chapter-54.md:319–321`); Karis answers from the coping (`chapter-54.md:323`). This is spatially consistent with Brom's fall outside the chamber, Oryn reaching him, his movement to the sill and his supported exit (`chapter-54.md:143–175, 291–321`), and with the source scene's separation of Brom on the floor from Karis on the coping. His subsequent wound remains the reopened shoulder, mended a second time and then bound.
+- The protected "Twice" unit runs intact through "Arm" / "No" (`chapter-55.md:29`), and no later speech asks for or supplies a third mending.
+- Teague's weir slip is forfeited, not paid or set (`chapter-56.md:71–77`).
+- Karis laid the ruler herself; no test was set for her (`chapter-57.md:73`).
+- The fourth line is not found by Lira's sigil or boot. The repaired approach says the iron remains below her (`chapter-58.md:149`), and she is finally one pace above it with her hand on the bow strap (`chapter-58.md:205`).
+- The old woman's knee was mended at Millrace in chapter 47. The repaired coda now says so, locates her winter stay at her daughter's Thornwater hearth, preserves Oryn's after-thaw promise, and has her walk over on the mended knee without accepting the delay (`chapter-60.md:151–161`).
+
+### Light pass — RESOLVED
+
+Every chapter remains within the brief's requested bands: mean sentence length 13.51–14.18 words, sentences of forty or more words 3.4–4.2%, and 882.7–1,022.8 words per scene.
+
+The flags ruled KEEP in the brief remain settled and have not been reopened.
+
+## (2) Continuity
+
+### Binding Book 7 ending
+
+All items in `BOOK_MAP.md` §1 "Ending" are on the page:
+
+- **Fourth site:** it is unnamed, outside-only and unentered. The silhouette remains ambiguous (`chapter-58.md:125–131`); Lira stops one pace above the iron (`chapter-58.md:151–161, 205`); no hand touches it, no sigil is lost or returned, and no Path tests its effect. There is no watch-post and no age or date is assigned to the cordon. The size is stated in yards and strides (`chapter-58.md:195`).
+- **Line and maker limits:** Karis says only "as near as this skin can show" (`chapter-57.md:77`), without a compass bearing. Her hypothesis remains unstated. The only permitted maker statements survive: "Someone made this pattern" (`chapter-60.md:251`) and the protected final line about a map line drawn before the registry (`chapter-60.md:255–265`). Nothing is decoded.
+- **Count and cash:** the sequence is fully shown—trial uncounted; twenty-three; Hall readings twenty-four and twenty-five; held Anchor point twenty-six; Tide on Oryn, asked and granted, twenty-seven (`chapter-53.md:387–389`; `chapter-54.md`; `chapter-55.md:163, 235–239, 301`). The final cash is ninety-six (`chapter-60.md:11`), supported by the movement's shown receipts and expenditures.
+- **Lowmarch records:** Pike has nine lines and no season number, and the five are eleventh (`chapter-59.md:177–215`). The kit is itemised on the table—the tarred case, knotted cord, stake thirty-two with mark and bright unused point, mallet, shut ledger and three boxes (`chapter-60.md:17–29`). There are fifty-two sheets: eleven, twenty-nine and twelve (`chapter-60.md:21–25`). The case stays shut.
+- **Calendar and correspondence:** first snow falls on the 129th (`chapter-59.md:47–51`); the last ferry runs on the 130th (`chapter-60.md:47–95`); two letters go west, to Hesk and Vell, while Ephram's is deferred to the first boat after the thaw (`chapter-60.md:75–87`).
+- **Terms and bodies:** Teague's line is "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes" / "Noted" (`chapter-59.md:219–225`); Pike's fence exchange is "Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road" / "Ours" (`chapter-59.md:229–239`). Lira's first-snow order stands, her right ankle is unmended, and her left arm holds nothing. Brom's shoulder is bound after the second mending, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow stays with Lira with one bolt (`chapter-58.md:19–27`; `chapter-59.md:23–49`; `chapter-60.md:141–147, 231–235`).
+- **Final protected material:** the inventory (`chapter-60.md:35–41`) and closing (`chapter-60.md:255–265`) match their protected sources exactly, including the binding #48 wording. The closing is the last text in the book. The #49 wording is untouched; #51 remains untouched in chapter 44 and is not explained here.
+- **Instrument result:** both straightedges read true in Cael's hand (`chapter-60.md:239–245`).
+
+### Knowledge, consent and reserved truths
+
+- The three self-readings occur on three distinct calendar days: the 102nd, the night of the 119th, and before light on the 120th. The last pair are made distinct on the page by the dated transition and confirmed by "three days, night between each" (`chapter-55.md:169–219`). Oryn reads Cael only after "May I?" / "Yes" (`chapter-55.md:235–239`). The debt is declared paid (`chapter-55.md:283`). Oryn has not forgiven the taking of the tenth (`chapter-60.md:125`).
+- Teague neither reads Cael nor asks to; the wrist remains untouched, and the prose states "Nor did he ask" (`chapter-56.md:163–171`). Nothing endorses or excuses the original taking.
+- "The still place" is presented as a located finding already named in the log, not coined here: shape and sensation only, with "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log" and no theory (`chapter-57.md:191–209`).
+- Shadow is unused. Karis's hypothesis remains unstated. Teague's crew remains unnamed. No new proper name appears. The prose is season-blind and uses yards and feet. Lira's arm is inert at the Hall; the coda no longer re-explains; the trial is never counted; the case is shut; and there is no decoding.
+
+### Prior and later continuity
+
+Chapter 47 bears out the repaired Thornwater staging: the old woman's knee is mended before she leaves Millrace (`chapter-47.md:61–85`). Chapter 44's protected #51 line remains intact (`chapter-44.md:219`).
+
+Every bullet of `LEDGER-RULINGS.md` is borne out except the last sentence of its Oryn bullet. The ruling says, at `LEDGER-RULINGS.md:10`, "Her mule and the grey jenny are with the crew." The surviving prose instead has Oryn take the left road (`chapter-58.md:37`) while five people continue with one mule (`chapter-58.md:59`), then shows Oryn travelling with the grey jenny (`chapter-60.md:103`) and reaching Thornwater on it (`chapter-60.md:133`). Chapter 47 established the division: Oryn takes Millrace's grey jenny; her brown mule remains with the crew. Coordinator correction: **Her brown mule is with the crew; the mill's grey jenny is with Oryn.** This is a ruling-file error, not a manuscript defect.
+
+The Book 8 opening documents are also still unreconciled in the precise ways anticipated by `plan-audit.md`; Book 7's prose matches the intended seam. Before Book 8 drafting/release, correct these stale artifacts:
+
+- `book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22` names "autumn," says "nothing owed," and `:24` says Oryn still owes a full reading; `:25` uses "Spring"; `:26` gives the fourth site's radius as 400 m.
+- `book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:13` repeats "autumn"; `:29` repeats 400 m; `:30` says Cael's "Path" works inside quiet ground although he has no Path; `:49` says nothing is owed; `:83,95` carry the reading as still owed.
+
+The Book 7 close instead has a paid consent debt, 440 yards and two strides, an after-thaw term, the ferryman's rope still owed, and Ephram's reply deferred. These are downstream metadata fixes only.
